+/// Turn Box3D's clock on or off, for every world. It is on by default. Off, b3GetTicks and the
+/// b3GetMilliseconds functions read no clock and return zero, so a world's profile reads zero, no
+/// stall is logged, and a step makes no system calls for the time (in WebAssembly each is a call
+/// out of the module). The simulation never reads the clock, so it steps the same either way.
+/// Change it only between steps: the threads a step runs on read it.
+B3_API void b3EnableTimer( bool flag );
+
+/// Is Box3D's clock on?
+B3_API bool b3IsTimerEnabled( void );
+
 // Used to detect bad values. In float mode positions greater than about 16km have precision
 // problems, so 100km is a safe limit. Large world mode keeps coordinates accurate much farther
 // from the origin, so the sanity limit widens to keep valid far-field positions from tripping it.
